cdk: forget the grab cursor on grabs with an explicit cursor

A successful grab remembers the cursor it was taken with only when it
was taken without an explicit cursor: when a grab with an explicit
cursor is taken while a cursorless grab is still remembered, the
remembered image survives until the ungrab, and windows applying their
NULL cursor while the explicit grab is active redefine that remembered
image instead of inheriting the explicit cursor of the grab window,
which the server shows on the grab window while the grab lasts.

Remember the cursor the grab was taken with on every successful grab:
cursorless grabs keep remembering the frozen or arrow image, and grabs
with an explicit cursor remember None, so those windows walk up to the
grab window and inherit its explicit cursor.
